      "id": "pre_graph_reduction",
      "kind": "planned_module",
      "stage": 3,
      "status": "pilot_implemented_pending_test",
      "description": "Architecture revision requested by user: before initial similarity graph, process logical 10000-row chunks with fixed preprocessing and local unsupervised KNN-based grouping, retaining approximately 10% actual representative records (1000 per full chunk). This is distinct from later structure-aware graph compression. KNN grouping algorithm not yet specified or implemented; KNN alone is not clustering. Preserve rare/isolated behaviors via label-free novelty/coverage allocation, avoid density-only selection, retain source-to-representative mapping, multiplicity, distances and provenance; flag uncovered records rather than silently discarding them. Labels only for evaluation. Compare rare-pattern recall, coverage error, downstream PR-AUC/recall, cross-chunk neighbor recall, runtime/RAM against unreduced and random baselines. Fixed similarity threshold strictly >0.85; current ZCA provisional, mixed formula parity pending. Full chunk pair count 49,995,000 versus 499,500 for 1000 representatives; 99% reduction in graph-stage comparisons only, not end-to-end KNN cost. Use bounded block or indexed candidate search, no full dataset dense matrix. Cross-chunk representative edges must remain possible. Two successive 10% reductions would retain 1% overall; second-stage budget must be separately validated. Protect mapping and raw security data locally; do not publish raw records or identifiers. Pilot before acceptance; exact grouping, rarity budget, mapping format and cross-file coalescing pending.",
      "path": "preprocessing/reduction.py"
    },
